1
00:00:10,302 --> 00:00:11,303
[Squad Member] Over here!

2
00:00:11,303 --> 00:00:12,679
-I think I found someone.
-Units 11 and 16.

3
00:00:12,679 --> 00:00:13,680
-Hurry.
-Hurry up

4
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,349
and search for survivors.

5
00:00:15,349 --> 00:00:17,267
The rest of you, you're coming with me.

6
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:18,268
[Squad] Sir.

7
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:19,770
[Yasochika] Leave the dead for later.

8
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:21,730
The wounded are our priority right now.

9
00:00:22,648 --> 00:00:24,107
-He didn't make it.
-That one looks critical.

10
00:00:24,107 --> 00:00:25,859
Take him to room 203, hurry.

11
00:00:28,987 --> 00:00:32,115
(Isane sighing)

12
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:35,536
Captain Unohana, was it
really the right thing

13
00:00:35,536 --> 00:00:38,705
for us to do, to remain
here in the barracks?

14
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:41,208
We might've saved more
lives if we'd been out there

15
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:42,668
-with the rest of the-
-Isane.

16
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:46,672
We can't let our feelings
dictate our actions.

17
00:00:46,672 --> 00:00:48,882
The natural reaction
would have been for us

18
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:50,676
to leave our posts out of concern.

19
00:00:52,219 --> 00:00:54,888
But I know you are not so
short-sighted that I need

20
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:57,975
to explain to you why that
would have been wrong.

21
00:00:57,975 --> 00:01:00,060
We both know you're wiser than that.

22
00:01:01,562 --> 00:01:03,146
Right.

23
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:05,315
I'm sorry, ma'am (sobs), forgive me!

24
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:09,069
There's no need for tears, Isane.

25
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:12,489
"Do not leave the Squad
4 barracks," he told us.

26
00:01:12,489 --> 00:01:13,824
"No matter what."

27
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:18,662
Who knew that when the Head
Captain gave us those orders

28
00:01:19,413 --> 00:01:21,915
they would be the last
that he would ever give?

29
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:26,003
(rain pattering)

30
00:01:32,634 --> 00:01:37,639
("Scar" by Tatsuya Kitani)

31
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:51,904
BLEACH: THOUSAND-YEAR BLOOD WAR

32
00:01:51,904 --> 00:01:56,909
♪ The blue skies above
are hopelessly clear ♪

33
00:01:56,909 --> 00:02:01,914
♪ At my wit's end, I feel
a growing frustration ♪

34
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:06,835
♪ As if to laugh at us hopeless cowards ♪

35
00:02:07,169 --> 00:02:10,297
♪ Countless eyes stare at us ♪

36
00:02:11,048 --> 00:02:16,929
♪ This soul of mine breaks again and again ♪

37
00:02:17,221 --> 00:02:20,098
♪ All I can do is hold it tight ♪

38
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:26,438
♪ Until the day it turns to ash ♪

39
00:02:26,438 --> 00:02:29,358
♪ I've absorbed all of this sorrow ♪

40
00:02:29,358 --> 00:02:33,987
♪ It has shaped me, painted me ♪

41
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:36,615
♪ But that's how we got here, right? ♪

42
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:41,537
♪ One step at a time, just like breathing ♪

43
00:02:41,537 --> 00:02:44,331
♪ These countless scars on my palm ♪

44
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:46,333
♪ That no longer fade ♪

45
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:50,003
♪ Are my badge, my story ♪

46
00:02:50,254 --> 00:02:54,091
♪ I faced the fear and shred it to pieces ♪

47
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:57,177
♪ And let it walk beside me once more ♪

48
00:02:57,177 --> 00:03:01,849
BLEACH: THOUSAND-YEAR BLOOD WAR

49
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:07,187
-("Scar" by Tatsuya Kitani)
-(singing in Japanese)

50
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:19,116
Kisuke Urahara wanted you
to know he's alive and well.

51
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:21,743
And that Orihime Inoue
and Yasutora Sado

52
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:23,287
are both safe, too.

53
00:03:23,287 --> 00:03:24,454
That's about it, Sir.

54
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:26,456
We don't have any more
details than that.

55
00:03:27,374 --> 00:03:28,375
All right.

56
00:03:29,126 --> 00:03:30,377
What?

57
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:32,129
That's a goddamn lie!

58
00:03:32,129 --> 00:03:33,088
There's no way.

59
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:35,132
No way Captain Zaraki lost to that guy!

60
00:03:35,132 --> 00:03:36,466
[Nurse] You need to calm down.

61
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:37,718
-Please.
-I need to see him!

62
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:38,760
-Captain!
-Ichigo.

63
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,929
You need some proper
medical treatment as well.

64
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:42,472
Why don't you come along with me.

65
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:44,308
Nah, I'm okay.

66
00:03:44,308 --> 00:03:46,810
They already looked me
over and bandaged me up.

67
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:48,312
Come on, I'm not just talking about

68
00:03:48,312 --> 00:03:49,521
those scratches on your face!

69
00:03:49,521 --> 00:03:52,065
I can tell you've been
seriously wounded!

70
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:53,483
Ichigo.

71
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:56,320
Rukia and Abarai just
got out of surgery.

72
00:03:57,279 --> 00:03:58,572
TRAUMA ROOM

73
00:03:58,572 --> 00:04:00,532
They're no longer in critical condition.

74
00:04:00,532 --> 00:04:01,742
They're stable now.

75
00:04:03,577 --> 00:04:05,412
Just call me if you need anything.

76
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:10,167
Ichigo.

77
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:11,168
Rukia!

78
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:13,212
Hey, you shouldn't even be talking.

79
00:04:11,418 --> 00:04:13,253
[Squad Member] This came for you, Sir.

80
00:04:13,212 --> 00:04:15,422
She just said we're
in stable condition,

81
00:04:15,422 --> 00:04:17,174
or have you gone deaf.

82
00:04:17,174 --> 00:04:18,675
On top of being dumb?

83
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:20,677
Dumb huh?

84
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:22,930
Sounds like your mouth
is working just fine.

85
00:04:24,181 --> 00:04:25,182
(heart monitor beeping)

86
00:04:25,182 --> 00:04:30,020
Ichigo, I knew you'd come to
help defend the Soul Society.

87
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:31,605
Thank you.

88
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:33,232
Of course I came.

89
00:04:33,232 --> 00:04:34,441
A little late, though.

90
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:36,693
I can't say I was very much help.

91
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:38,070
Shut up.

92
00:04:38,070 --> 00:04:41,281
You drove off the leader
of the enemy's forces.

93
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:43,116
If you hadn't done what you did,

94
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:45,619
things would've gotten
a whole lot worse.

95
00:04:45,619 --> 00:04:48,747
So hold your head up
high, you damn idiot.

96
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:50,207
[Ichigo] If you say so.

97
00:04:50,207 --> 00:04:51,625
(Rukia chuckling)

98
00:04:51,625 --> 00:04:53,460
Pardon the intrusion, Sir.

99
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:55,379
Captain Kurotsuchi wants to see you,

100
00:04:55,379 --> 00:04:56,797
regarding your Zanpakuto.

101
00:04:58,048 --> 00:05:00,592
-(rain pattering)
-(worrisome music)

102
00:05:00,592 --> 00:05:01,927
[Shinji] So typical.

103
00:05:01,927 --> 00:05:03,136
He's always running off somewhere,

104
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:05,264
no matter what the situation is.

105
00:05:05,264 --> 00:05:06,974
I wish he'd sit still and think

106
00:05:06,974 --> 00:05:08,892
of his own well-being for once.

107
00:05:10,561 --> 00:05:11,979
Captain Hirako,

108
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:15,315
did Ichigo seem different to you?

109
00:05:15,649 --> 00:05:17,484
He seemed troubled.

110
00:05:17,484 --> 00:05:19,820
Yeah, I couldn't help
noticing that as well.

111
00:05:20,654 --> 00:05:23,490
Though to be fair, his
Zanpakuto was broken.

112
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:26,910
He's exhausted and disappointed
he couldn't do more.

113
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:28,954
But I wouldn't worry
about him too much.

114
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:32,332
I don't know.

115
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:34,334
I think there's more to it than that.

116
00:05:36,336 --> 00:05:39,506
It seems like he's dealing
with something else.

117
00:05:39,506 --> 00:05:42,426
Something serious that
he's hiding from us.

118
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:45,929
(gentle music)

119
00:05:47,514 --> 00:05:50,767
[Jushiro] The Head Captain's
body has yet to be found.

120
00:05:52,019 --> 00:05:54,688
The enemy destroyed virtually everything.

121
00:05:57,608 --> 00:05:59,610
I have an update, Sir.

122
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:02,321
It appears that Squad
Captain Byakuya Kuchiki

123
00:06:02,321 --> 00:06:06,116
as well as Kenpachi Zaraki
have both managed to survive.

124
00:06:06,116 --> 00:06:08,785
But they have yet to
regain consciousness.

125
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:10,704
It's unlikely they will be able to return

126
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:12,873
to their duties any time soon.

127
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:15,375
In fact, they may never
regain consciousness again,

128
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:16,877
-it would seem-
-Get out!

129
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:19,296
We've had enough grim
tidings for one day.

130
00:06:19,296 --> 00:06:20,589
Where have you been?

131
00:06:20,589 --> 00:06:23,300
Haven't you heard we lost
the Head Captain, you fool?

132
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,469
How much more bad news
are we supposed to take?

133
00:06:25,469 --> 00:06:26,470
Get a grip.

134
00:06:26,470 --> 00:06:27,471
It's embarrassing.

135
00:06:27,471 --> 00:06:28,555
[Soi] Get a grip?

136
00:06:28,555 --> 00:06:30,057
That's easy for you to say!

137
00:06:30,057 --> 00:06:31,975
You guys have always
held a grudge against

138
00:06:31,975 --> 00:06:33,644
the Head Captain all these years!

139
00:06:33,644 --> 00:06:35,187
Don't you dare.

140
00:06:35,187 --> 00:06:36,605
Enough, Soi Fon!

141
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:39,233
Do you think you're the
only one who feels shattered

142
00:06:39,233 --> 00:06:40,234
by our loss?

143
00:06:40,234 --> 00:06:41,235
(Soi gasping)

144
00:06:41,527 --> 00:06:42,903
Now, now.

145
00:06:42,903 --> 00:06:44,821
-No fighting, no fighting.
-(hands clapping)

146
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:47,407
Play nice, everyone.

147
00:06:47,407 --> 00:06:50,577
If Old Man Yama was here to
see us squabbling like this,

148
00:06:50,577 --> 00:06:53,205
he'd give us all a
good smack on the head.

149
00:06:53,205 --> 00:06:55,832
Nor would he want
us standing around

150
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:58,502
bawling our heads off over his memory.

151
00:06:58,502 --> 00:07:00,003
Shunsui, you bastard.

152
00:07:00,003 --> 00:07:02,506
Remember what our purpose is.

153
00:07:02,506 --> 00:07:05,050
The Thirteen Court
Guard Squads aren't here

154
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:07,094
to mourn the Soul Society.

155
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:11,598
Our only job is to
protect the Soul Society.

156
00:07:12,683 --> 00:07:14,768
Or at least what's left of it.

157
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:18,272
So let's all just try and keep
moving forward, shall we?

158
00:07:19,356 --> 00:07:20,941
You can't fix it?

159
00:07:20,941 --> 00:07:22,025
Why can't you?

160
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:24,194
What do you do when your
Zanpakuto gets broken?

161
00:07:24,194 --> 00:07:26,613
Are you really telling me
you can't fix your own?

162
00:07:26,613 --> 00:07:28,115
When will you learn?

163
00:07:28,115 --> 00:07:32,536
I have never fixed my Zanpakuto,
I have merely modified it.

164
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:35,706
The only thing that
can fix a Zanpakuto

165
00:07:35,706 --> 00:07:38,709
is its owner's own mind
and Spiritual Pressure,

166
00:07:38,709 --> 00:07:40,711
and enough time to
infuse them both

167
00:07:40,711 --> 00:07:42,546
into the Zanpakuto itself.

168
00:07:42,546 --> 00:07:44,590
That's the only way.

169
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:46,592
(sighs) Okay, fine.

170
00:07:46,592 --> 00:07:48,886
So what you're saying is,
I have to take it back

171
00:07:48,886 --> 00:07:50,637
and fix the damn thing myself.

172
00:07:50,637 --> 00:07:51,889
Not quite.

173
00:07:51,889 --> 00:07:53,432
I hadn't finished my explanation.

174
00:07:53,432 --> 00:07:54,474
Huh?

175
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,727
That only applies to Shikai.

176
00:07:56,727 --> 00:07:58,312
If we're talking about the destruction

177
00:07:58,312 --> 00:08:01,982
of a Zanpakuto's Bankai,
then that's a bit trickier.

178
00:08:01,982 --> 00:08:04,234
Because once destroyed,
a Bankai can never

179
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:06,486
in fact be restored, I'm sorry to say.

180
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:07,487
What?

181
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:08,488
Wait a minute.

182
00:08:09,031 --> 00:08:11,617
But then, what's that mean?

183
00:08:11,617 --> 00:08:13,285
(communicator beeping)

184
00:08:13,285 --> 00:08:14,620
Yes, I'm here.

185
00:08:15,829 --> 00:08:17,414
(door whooshing)

186
00:08:17,414 --> 00:08:18,415
(Kon screaming)

187
00:08:18,415 --> 00:08:20,000
-Get away from me.
-Come back here, you.

188
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,585
-Kon?
-[Squad Member] Get him!

189
00:08:21,585 --> 00:08:24,796
What the heck is Kon doing
here in the Soul Society?

190
00:08:25,297 --> 00:08:26,840
-(door whooshing)
-I see.

191
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,592
Just as I thought.

192
00:08:28,592 --> 00:08:29,843
Very well.

193
00:08:29,843 --> 00:08:32,304
-I'm headed there now.
-Huh?

194
00:08:32,304 --> 00:08:35,182
You can come with me, Ichigo Kurosaki.

195
00:08:35,182 --> 00:08:36,642
We're expecting visitors.

196
00:08:36,642 --> 00:08:38,352
And if I have to meet them,

197
00:08:38,352 --> 00:08:40,103
you should have to meet them, too.

198
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:43,857
The great Squad Zero is on its way.

199
00:08:47,945 --> 00:08:49,613
-Shinji!
-Huh?

200
00:08:49,613 --> 00:08:51,532
Oh, you've come to
welcome them, too?

201
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:54,159
You might regret this, Ichigo.

202
00:08:55,369 --> 00:08:58,121
Why's this Squad Zero coming now?

203
00:08:58,121 --> 00:09:02,125
I mean after the Seireitei's
been completely annihilated?

204
00:09:02,125 --> 00:09:04,294
Where have they been all this time?

205
00:09:04,294 --> 00:09:05,879
In the Royal Palace.

206
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:09,216
Okay, but isn't that within the Seireitei?

207
00:09:09,216 --> 00:09:11,802
Remember how those
walls fell out of the sky

208
00:09:11,802 --> 00:09:13,512
when you first came here?

209
00:09:13,512 --> 00:09:14,680
(Ichigo gasping)

210
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:16,515
Those walls have remained down,

211
00:09:16,515 --> 00:09:19,142
forming a barrier around
this area, ever since you

212
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:20,978
and your friends got here.

213
00:09:20,978 --> 00:09:22,729
The walls were only ever intended

214
00:09:22,729 --> 00:09:25,566
to surround the Seireitei
during emergencies.

215
00:09:26,650 --> 00:09:28,902
Why is it then, they're
still down here,

216
00:09:28,902 --> 00:09:31,655
instead of where they
should be up in the sky,

217
00:09:31,655 --> 00:09:33,490
protecting the Royal Palace?

218
00:09:33,490 --> 00:09:34,491
(Ichigo gasping)

219
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:35,742
Look, here they are.

220
00:09:35,742 --> 00:09:36,743
(Ichigo gasping)

221
00:09:38,579 --> 00:09:41,373
(ground rumbling)

222
00:09:44,877 --> 00:09:46,170
What is that?

223
00:09:46,170 --> 00:09:47,713
Tenchuren.

224
00:09:47,713 --> 00:09:50,257
Squad Zero uses it to get around in.

225
00:09:51,425 --> 00:09:54,386
It has plenty of room
for five squad members.

226
00:09:54,386 --> 00:09:55,387
[Ichigo] What?

227
00:09:55,387 --> 00:09:56,722
There's only five?

228
00:09:56,722 --> 00:09:59,016
[Shunsui] It's a squad of captains only.

229
00:09:59,016 --> 00:10:01,351
-Five of 'em.
-(door rumbling)

230
00:10:01,351 --> 00:10:03,854
But the combined
power of those five

231
00:10:05,063 --> 00:10:09,776
is greater than that of all the
Thirteen Court Guard Squads.

232
00:10:09,776 --> 00:10:12,613
(uplifting music)

233
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:27,961
(ground rumbling)

234
00:10:29,171 --> 00:10:30,172
(flag flying)

235
00:10:30,172 --> 00:10:33,717
(dramatic music)

236
00:10:35,177 --> 00:10:36,553
Hell, yeah, that's right!

237
00:10:36,553 --> 00:10:40,390
We're here, drink it
in, we are finally here!

238
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:43,894
The one and only Squad
Zero is in the house!

239
00:10:43,894 --> 00:10:46,188
Long time no see, you rookies!

240
00:10:46,188 --> 00:10:47,773
How've you been keeping
yourselves, huh?

241
00:10:47,773 --> 00:10:48,815
Have you been eating right,

242
00:10:48,815 --> 00:10:50,651
-getting enough sleep,
-I can't say these guys

243
00:10:50,651 --> 00:10:52,486
are exactly what I pictured they'd be.

244
00:10:52,486 --> 00:10:53,570
-(hand thudding)
-(Shinji yelling)

245
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:55,239
What the hell was that for?

246
00:10:55,239 --> 00:10:58,033
It's been a while, hasn't it, Shinji?

247
00:10:58,033 --> 00:11:00,577
Hiyori isn't with you
today? How rare!

248
00:11:00,577 --> 00:11:01,537
It's been a while?

249
00:11:01,537 --> 00:11:03,163
I don't even know you.

250
00:11:03,163 --> 00:11:04,248
Wait.

251
00:11:04,248 --> 00:11:05,499
Hiyori?

252
00:11:05,499 --> 00:11:07,543
Have you forgotten who I am?

253
00:11:07,543 --> 00:11:08,544
It's me, Kirio!

254
00:11:08,544 --> 00:11:09,545
Remember?

255
00:11:09,545 --> 00:11:11,255
M-Miss Kirio?

256
00:11:11,255 --> 00:11:13,423
Whoa, you've, you've changed.

257
00:11:13,423 --> 00:11:15,008
You look completely different!

258
00:11:15,008 --> 00:11:17,427
Oh, Shinji, stop your teasing!

259
00:11:17,427 --> 00:11:19,596
I haven't changed all that much.

260
00:11:19,596 --> 00:11:22,099
-(stomach growling)
-Oh, I am starving!

261
00:11:26,562 --> 00:11:29,314
(chuckles) I bet you're happy
to see me again, Unohana.

262
00:11:29,314 --> 00:11:30,315
Are ya?

263
00:11:30,315 --> 00:11:32,401
So anyway, I'm curious,
have you been putting

264
00:11:32,401 --> 00:11:35,153
all those healing techniques
I taught you to good use?

265
00:11:35,153 --> 00:11:36,446
Yes, of course

266
00:11:36,446 --> 00:11:37,865
Ya sure about that?

267
00:11:37,865 --> 00:11:40,284
'Cause from what I heard,
you guys ended up having

268
00:11:40,284 --> 00:11:42,578
to bury a lot of your squad members.

269
00:11:42,578 --> 00:11:45,247
How do you explain that, hm?

270
00:11:45,247 --> 00:11:46,456
(Retsu sighing)

271
00:11:46,456 --> 00:11:47,666
Enough of that!

272
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:50,460
I know you wanna kiss
and catch up, but save it

273
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,963
'cause we've got bigger fish to fry!

274
00:11:52,963 --> 00:11:54,464
(Tenjiro groaning)

275
00:11:54,464 --> 00:11:57,885
Well, I see no one in Squad
Zero's changed very much,

276
00:11:57,885 --> 00:11:59,636
have they, Osho?

277
00:11:59,636 --> 00:12:03,807
So, what's made you decide to
bless us with your presence?

278
00:12:04,725 --> 00:12:06,101
Hmm.

279
00:12:06,101 --> 00:12:08,896
So this is Ichigo Kurosaki, huh?

280
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:12,065
The Soul King ordered us to come

281
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:16,486
and start rebuilding the
Thirteen Court Guard squads.

282
00:12:16,486 --> 00:12:18,989
And the first order of business

283
00:12:18,989 --> 00:12:22,075
is to take Ichigo back with us.

284
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:23,660
You gotta be kidding!

285
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:25,537
The great Squad Zero, huh?

286
00:12:25,537 --> 00:12:27,247
Cooling your heels up in the sky

287
00:12:27,247 --> 00:12:29,583
while the Seireitei
was being destroyed!

288
00:12:29,583 --> 00:12:32,002
And now you think you can
just come floating down here

289
00:12:32,002 --> 00:12:33,003
and pick up the pieces?

290
00:12:33,003 --> 00:12:35,255
What is this, some kind of joke?

291
00:12:36,423 --> 00:12:39,259
[Ichibe] Right, well,
anyway, as I was saying,

292
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:40,302
-our orders are to-
-Hey.

293
00:12:40,302 --> 00:12:41,595
Shut up, will ya?

294
00:12:42,763 --> 00:12:44,348
What kind of move was that?

295
00:12:44,348 --> 00:12:47,226
The only joke around here is you.

296
00:12:47,643 --> 00:12:49,937
The Thirteen Court Guard Squads.

297
00:12:49,937 --> 00:12:52,606
Remind me what your job even is.

298
00:12:52,606 --> 00:12:55,609
I know our job's to
protect the Royal Palace.

299
00:12:55,609 --> 00:12:58,862
I always thought your job
was to protect the Seireitei.

300
00:12:58,862 --> 00:13:01,615
What kind of Court Guard
goes crying for help

301
00:13:01,615 --> 00:13:04,618
after failing at the
one job they've got?

302
00:13:04,618 --> 00:13:06,578
You're not even worthy of the name.

303
00:13:07,996 --> 00:13:08,997
-(fist thudding)
-(Tenjiro yelling)

304
00:13:08,997 --> 00:13:10,332
Hey, watch the hair!

305
00:13:10,999 --> 00:13:12,000
(Tenjiro thudding)

306
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,378
I told you to save all that for later.

307
00:13:14,378 --> 00:13:17,548
Let's just finish gathering
up what we came here to get.

308
00:13:17,548 --> 00:13:18,882
[Senjumaru] No need.

309
00:13:18,882 --> 00:13:19,883
Hmm?

310
00:13:19,883 --> 00:13:21,009
I took care of it.

311
00:13:21,009 --> 00:13:23,887
Everything else on the list
of things we were sent to get

312
00:13:23,887 --> 00:13:25,514
is right here.

313
00:13:25,514 --> 00:13:28,559
-(dramatic music)
-(all gasping)

314
00:13:28,559 --> 00:13:31,228
That means the only
one remaining is you.

315
00:13:33,313 --> 00:13:35,649
Ichigo Kurosaki.

316
00:13:35,649 --> 00:13:37,484
Not possible.

317
00:13:37,484 --> 00:13:40,362
The three people you're
holding in those spheres

318
00:13:40,362 --> 00:13:42,322
are in absolutely no condition

319
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:44,366
to leave the Seireitei right now.

320
00:13:44,366 --> 00:13:47,077
I cannot allow you to
take them with you.

321
00:13:47,077 --> 00:13:48,078
Hmm.

322
00:13:48,537 --> 00:13:51,123
Their condition is the reason
we're taking them with us,

323
00:13:51,123 --> 00:13:52,124
in the first place.

324
00:13:53,333 --> 00:13:55,752
Hey, you know as well as anyone,

325
00:13:55,752 --> 00:13:57,504
you haven't got the healing chops

326
00:13:57,504 --> 00:13:59,506
to make those three
rookies well again.

327
00:14:00,924 --> 00:14:05,012
You know it's true,
don't you, Retsu?

328
00:14:05,012 --> 00:14:07,931
Besides, you have more
important things than healing

329
00:14:07,931 --> 00:14:09,391
to be focused on right now.

330
00:14:12,853 --> 00:14:16,106
So I see you broke into my lab.

331
00:14:16,106 --> 00:14:17,691
You haven't changed.

332
00:14:17,691 --> 00:14:20,903
You're just as disrespectful as ever.

333
00:14:20,903 --> 00:14:24,531
Well, well, if it isn't
my dear old friend Mayuri.

334
00:14:24,531 --> 00:14:26,283
It's a bit of an exaggeration

335
00:14:26,283 --> 00:14:28,410
to say that I broke into your lab.

336
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:30,871
The fact is, I was able to walk right in.

337
00:14:30,871 --> 00:14:33,749
I barely even had to touch the door.

338
00:14:33,749 --> 00:14:35,250
Really.

339
00:14:35,250 --> 00:14:37,920
It seems to me that security
has gotten a lot shabbier

340
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:39,421
since I was around.

341
00:14:39,421 --> 00:14:40,422
(Mayuri scoffing)

342
00:14:40,422 --> 00:14:42,216
Wait. Back up just a minute?

343
00:14:42,216 --> 00:14:44,635
Did you guys say you
wanted to take me too?

344
00:14:44,635 --> 00:14:46,428
My wounds are nothing!

345
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:48,639
I'll recover just fine
here in the Seireitei.

346
00:14:48,639 --> 00:14:49,806
Hmm.

347
00:14:49,806 --> 00:14:51,475
Yes, we know.

348
00:14:51,475 --> 00:14:55,312
But we'll be taking you for
an entirely different reason.

349
00:14:55,312 --> 00:14:56,772
And that is?

350
00:14:56,772 --> 00:14:58,649
[Kisuke] Hello there, everybody!

351
00:14:58,649 --> 00:15:01,109
Hey, sorry I didn't
get in touch sooner.

352
00:15:01,109 --> 00:15:03,153
I bet you were worried
about me, weren't you?

353
00:15:03,153 --> 00:15:06,573
Well, as you can see,
I'm fit as a fiddle!

354
00:15:06,573 --> 00:15:07,574
Hello?

355
00:15:07,574 --> 00:15:10,494
Wow, I was expecting a
little bit more of a welcome.

356
00:15:10,494 --> 00:15:11,912
-I mean-
-What's going on?

357
00:15:11,912 --> 00:15:13,413
Why did my head crack open?

358
00:15:13,413 --> 00:15:15,332
I've got light coming
out of my brain!

359
00:15:15,332 --> 00:15:16,959
-(Kon screaming)
-Ichigo!

360
00:15:16,959 --> 00:15:19,169
Oh, thank goodness
you're all right!

361
00:15:19,169 --> 00:15:21,255
Everything is okay over there, I hope?

362
00:15:21,255 --> 00:15:22,506
Just fine.

363
00:15:22,506 --> 00:15:23,507
How 'bout yourself?

364
00:15:23,507 --> 00:15:25,092
Are you doing all right?

365
00:15:25,092 --> 00:15:26,927
Yeah, I'm okay, don't worry.

366
00:15:28,512 --> 00:15:29,805
Ichigo!

367
00:15:29,805 --> 00:15:32,516
Oh man, am I glad you're safe.

368
00:15:32,516 --> 00:15:33,934
Right back at ya.

369
00:15:33,934 --> 00:15:36,478
I can't even begin to tell
ya how worried I've been.

370
00:15:36,478 --> 00:15:38,188
[Kisuke] Yeah, I know, I know.

371
00:15:38,188 --> 00:15:42,693
I wanted to contact you sooner,
but well a lot's happened.

372
00:15:42,693 --> 00:15:44,361
[Grimmjow] Hey, who are
you talking to in there?

373
00:15:44,361 --> 00:15:45,362
-Oh.
-Uh.

374
00:15:46,363 --> 00:15:48,031
Wait a second, that
sounds a lot like-

375
00:15:48,031 --> 00:15:49,616
[Grimmjow] Hey! I
know that voice!

376
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:51,034
[Kisuke] Orihime!

377
00:15:51,034 --> 00:15:52,327
Chad, help!

378
00:15:52,327 --> 00:15:53,287
[Grimmjow] Ichigo, you bastard!

379
00:15:53,287 --> 00:15:54,538
-I know you're in there!
-No, no.

380
00:15:54,538 --> 00:15:55,622
-He isn't in here, honest.
-Kisuke,

381
00:15:55,622 --> 00:15:56,623
what the hell's he doing there?

382
00:15:56,623 --> 00:15:57,624
What's goin' on?

383
00:15:57,624 --> 00:16:01,295
Anyway, as you can see,
we're all perfectly fine

384
00:16:01,295 --> 00:16:02,880
on this end, Ichigo.

385
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:06,383
So you just do what you have
to do, don't worry about us.

386
00:16:06,383 --> 00:16:09,553
It's okay to think about
yourself for a change.

387
00:16:09,553 --> 00:16:12,848
Go wherever your heart
tells you you should go.

388
00:16:12,848 --> 00:16:15,309
(Grimmjow yelling)

389
00:16:15,309 --> 00:16:18,312
Oh, and by the way, don't
give him a second thought.

390
00:16:18,312 --> 00:16:20,981
We've kind of come
to an arrangement.

391
00:16:20,981 --> 00:16:22,566
Well, see ya later!

392
00:16:25,736 --> 00:16:28,572
[Chad] Was it smart,
telling him that?

393
00:16:28,572 --> 00:16:29,698
Telling him what?

394
00:16:32,993 --> 00:16:34,494
Aah, I'm not worried about it,

395
00:16:34,494 --> 00:16:36,747
because if Ichigo does what
his heart tells him to do

396
00:16:36,747 --> 00:16:39,374
and nothing else I've
got a pretty good feeling

397
00:16:39,374 --> 00:16:40,834
that the world and all of us in it

398
00:16:40,834 --> 00:16:43,003
will be a lot better
off because of it.

399
00:16:43,170 --> 00:16:47,007
I mean, come on, you two should
know that better than I do.

400
00:16:49,426 --> 00:16:54,223
And believe me, the guy who
knows that better than anyone

401
00:16:54,223 --> 00:16:56,016
is Ichigo himself.

402
00:16:57,184 --> 00:16:58,769
[Ichigo] Hey, Baldy.

403
00:16:58,769 --> 00:17:01,188
Are you talking to me?

404
00:17:01,188 --> 00:17:03,607
[Ichigo] If I go to this
Royal Palace with you,

405
00:17:03,607 --> 00:17:06,276
will I be able to fix
my Tensa Zangetsu?

406
00:17:06,276 --> 00:17:07,945
Nope, that's impossible.

407
00:17:07,945 --> 00:17:10,697
Your sword can't be fixed.

408
00:17:10,697 --> 00:17:13,700
However, if you were to
come to the Royal Palace,

409
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:15,452
we could re-forge it into something

410
00:17:15,452 --> 00:17:17,579
resembling your original sword.

411
00:17:21,583 --> 00:17:22,584
-Fine.
-Hm?

412
00:17:24,378 --> 00:17:25,546
Let's go, then.

413
00:17:25,546 --> 00:17:27,130
The Royal Palace it is.

414
00:17:28,131 --> 00:17:29,174
All right.

415
00:17:29,174 --> 00:17:31,134
-“WELCOME TO KUKAKU SHIBA’S RESIDENCE”
-Stand by for launch!

416
00:17:31,718 --> 00:17:32,719
Huh?

417
00:17:33,637 --> 00:17:35,722
And lift off!

418
00:17:37,558 --> 00:17:41,645
[Ichigo] Aren't there any
seat belts on this thing?

419
00:17:43,272 --> 00:17:44,565
[Ganju] There he goes.

420
00:17:44,565 --> 00:17:47,818
Are you sure it was the
right thing to do, Sis?

421
00:17:47,818 --> 00:17:48,986
Yeah.

422
00:17:48,986 --> 00:17:51,238
If he doesn't go now, the Soul Society

423
00:17:51,238 --> 00:17:53,740
is doomed when the
next invasion comes.

424
00:17:55,242 --> 00:17:57,119
It's not like we had a choice.

425
00:17:58,370 --> 00:18:00,914
We had to let him go
even if that means

426
00:18:00,914 --> 00:18:02,666
making our Uncle sad.

427
00:18:05,502 --> 00:18:08,672
Right, everyone back to
Kukaku's Great Training Hall,

428
00:18:08,672 --> 00:18:09,840
on the double!

429
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:12,009
My brother's not going
to train himself.

430
00:18:12,009 --> 00:18:14,178
Don't forget who took
you in off the streets

431
00:18:14,178 --> 00:18:16,346
of the Rukon District.

432
00:18:16,346 --> 00:18:19,266
[Kugo] I hate the way she
keeps reminding us of that.

433
00:18:19,266 --> 00:18:20,642
[Giriko] You and me both.

434
00:18:20,642 --> 00:18:23,353
[Kukaku] Time for you
to step up, Ganju.

435
00:18:23,353 --> 00:18:24,938
You can complain all you want,

436
00:18:24,938 --> 00:18:27,191
but I'm throwing you
into the next battle.

437
00:18:28,275 --> 00:18:29,276
Got it.

438
00:18:32,196 --> 00:18:34,198
(ground rumbling)

439
00:18:34,198 --> 00:18:36,158
[Ichibe] You can get out now, Ichigo!

440
00:18:37,367 --> 00:18:38,368
We're here!

441
00:18:38,869 --> 00:18:41,205
THE ROYAL PALACE
The Royal Palace!

442
00:18:47,211 --> 00:18:49,796
(gentle music)

443
00:18:50,714 --> 00:18:52,132
So this is it.

444
00:18:52,132 --> 00:18:53,133
That's right!

445
00:18:53,133 --> 00:18:54,134
You're lucky.

446
00:18:54,134 --> 00:18:56,178
You might not be
aware of this, my boy,

447
00:18:56,178 --> 00:18:59,848
but Soul Reapers aren't
ordinarily allowed up here.

448
00:18:59,848 --> 00:19:03,519
But then, there's nothing
really ordinary about you,

449
00:19:03,519 --> 00:19:04,645
is there?

450
00:19:04,645 --> 00:19:06,688
So this is the place Aizen

451
00:19:06,688 --> 00:19:08,565
so desperately wanted to come to.

452
00:19:09,983 --> 00:19:11,318
Hey, wait a minute!

453
00:19:11,318 --> 00:19:12,319
Am I missing something?

454
00:19:12,319 --> 00:19:14,238
I thought you couldn't
get into the Royal Palace

455
00:19:14,238 --> 00:19:15,656
without the Ouken!

456
00:19:15,656 --> 00:19:17,741
(chuckles) It's here.

457
00:19:17,741 --> 00:19:20,327
Our bones are the Ouken.

458
00:19:20,327 --> 00:19:22,663
That's right, they were
transformed by the power

459
00:19:22,663 --> 00:19:25,082
of the Soul King when
we were selected by him

460
00:19:25,082 --> 00:19:27,334
to join Squad Zero.

461
00:19:27,334 --> 00:19:30,337
You see, there are only
two ways to gain entrance

462
00:19:30,337 --> 00:19:31,755
to the Royal Palace.

463
00:19:31,755 --> 00:19:35,259
Either we choose to allow you
in or you come in with us.

464
00:19:36,677 --> 00:19:40,013
Sosuke Aizen was trying
to make an imitation Ouken

465
00:19:40,013 --> 00:19:41,014
of his own.

466
00:19:41,014 --> 00:19:42,516
In other words, he was trying

467
00:19:42,516 --> 00:19:46,728
to use his own spiritual
powers to create clones of us.

468
00:19:46,728 --> 00:19:50,065
He wanted to make
himself into a new god.

469
00:19:50,065 --> 00:19:53,360
By killing the king, as
well as millions of others.

470
00:19:55,571 --> 00:19:57,447
Sosuke Aizen.

471
00:19:57,447 --> 00:20:00,075
He truly is evil personified.

472
00:20:01,034 --> 00:20:03,871
But know this, Ichigo Kurosaki,

473
00:20:05,289 --> 00:20:07,541
the Quincies you are now facing

474
00:20:07,541 --> 00:20:10,711
are an even greater
and more terrible evil.

475
00:20:10,711 --> 00:20:13,797
(Ichigo grunting)

476
00:20:13,797 --> 00:20:15,549
All right, ready?

477
00:20:15,549 --> 00:20:17,217
I'm gonna blast you off now!

478
00:20:17,217 --> 00:20:18,552
Stand right there!

479
00:20:18,552 --> 00:20:21,096
Don't move, or you'll die!

480
00:20:21,096 --> 00:20:23,056
Okay, here goes.

481
00:20:23,056 --> 00:20:24,808
Wait, hold on a second!

482
00:20:24,808 --> 00:20:25,809
What is it?

483
00:20:25,809 --> 00:20:27,311
I don't even know where
the hell I'm headed!

484
00:20:27,311 --> 00:20:29,229
Am I going to meet the Soul King?

485
00:20:29,229 --> 00:20:30,230
Huh?

486
00:20:30,230 --> 00:20:31,773
Come on, you're not serious, are ya?

487
00:20:31,773 --> 00:20:34,067
There's no way a punk
like you is ever gonna

488
00:20:34,067 --> 00:20:35,319
meet the Soul King.

489
00:20:35,319 --> 00:20:36,445
-What did I say
-Try explaining it

490
00:20:36,445 --> 00:20:37,487
-about the hair?
-to him properly!

491
00:20:37,821 --> 00:20:39,615
-THE ROYAL PALACE – MAIN ENTRANCE
-Now listen closely.

492
00:20:39,615 --> 00:20:41,825
Right now, we're at
the main entrance.

493
00:20:41,825 --> 00:20:43,869
-REIO GREATER PALACE
-Over there is the main shrine,

494
00:20:43,869 --> 00:20:45,746
the Reio Greater Palace.

495
00:20:45,746 --> 00:20:48,165
That's where the Soul King resides.

496
00:20:48,165 --> 00:20:49,875
-SQUAD ZERO RIDEN
-And those five disc-like structures

497
00:20:49,875 --> 00:20:53,504
floating around it are the Squad Zero Riden.

498
00:20:53,504 --> 00:20:55,797
Those are our castles.

499
00:20:55,797 --> 00:20:56,840
You got that?

500
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:58,675
You see, there's five of 'em.

501
00:20:58,675 --> 00:21:01,261
But forget the other
four, it's my Kirinden

502
00:21:01,261 --> 00:21:02,304
that you're coming to.

503
00:21:02,304 --> 00:21:04,348
Meaning you and your friends.

504
00:21:05,724 --> 00:21:06,725
“KIRINDEN”

505
00:21:07,351 --> 00:21:09,895
(Ichigo sighing)

506
00:21:09,895 --> 00:21:11,230
[Ichigo] What the hell is this?

507
00:21:11,230 --> 00:21:12,397
[Tenjiro] What's it look like?

508
00:21:12,397 --> 00:21:14,358
Haven't you ever seen
a hot spring, before.

509
00:21:14,358 --> 00:21:15,984
[Ichigo] Why are they underwater?

510
00:21:15,984 --> 00:21:17,611
You're gonna drown them!

511
00:21:17,611 --> 00:21:20,322
-Look, he's bleeding!
-Calm down.

512
00:21:20,322 --> 00:21:22,032
I'm soaking them in the hot spring

513
00:21:22,032 --> 00:21:24,785
in order to drain out their
damaged Spiritual Pressure

514
00:21:24,785 --> 00:21:26,119
along with their blood.

515
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:27,955
Damaged Spiritual Pressure?

516
00:21:27,955 --> 00:21:31,333
You see that boiling,
red-hot spring over there?

517
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:33,710
-“BLOOD POND HELL”
-[Ichigo] (gasps) Blood Pond Hell?

518
00:21:33,710 --> 00:21:36,213
[Tenjiro] Right, Blood Pond Hell.

519
00:21:36,213 --> 00:21:40,676
So we're gonna take Byakuya
here, who's all drained out

520
00:21:40,676 --> 00:21:42,135
and toss him in there!

521
00:21:42,135 --> 00:21:43,345
Hey, what are you doing?

522
00:21:43,345 --> 00:21:44,805
You're gonna kill the guy.

523
00:21:44,805 --> 00:21:47,140
Would you please calm the hell down?

524
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:49,518
I draw out their blood
in White Bone Hell

525
00:21:49,518 --> 00:21:52,312
and replenish it in Blood Pond Hell.

526
00:21:52,312 --> 00:21:54,565
Repeat the process a few times

527
00:21:54,565 --> 00:21:56,692
and eventually, every
drop of bad blood

528
00:21:56,692 --> 00:21:58,193
and Spiritual Pressure in their bodies

529
00:21:58,193 --> 00:22:01,238
will be swapped out for
pure, hot, healthy water.

530
00:22:01,238 --> 00:22:02,698
That's the way I heal 'em.

531
00:22:03,073 --> 00:22:04,741
I find it a little hard to believe

532
00:22:04,741 --> 00:22:05,742
that this thing is gonna-

533
00:22:05,742 --> 00:22:07,369
Just shut up and start soaking.

534
00:22:07,369 --> 00:22:09,246
For the kind of injuries you have,

535
00:22:10,414 --> 00:22:11,915
one night should do it.

536
00:22:11,915 --> 00:22:14,877
That's all it'll take to make
you twice as good as new.

537
00:22:14,877 --> 00:22:16,670
-“HOT SPRING DEMON” – TENJIRO KIRINJI
-(dramatic music)

538
00:22:19,089 --> 00:22:24,094
("Saihate" by SennaRin)

539
00:22:24,136 --> 00:22:27,306
♪ Everything we had left behind ♪

540
00:22:27,306 --> 00:22:31,518
♪ Our breaths blending as mist ♪

541
00:22:31,518 --> 00:22:36,148
♪ without form or expression ♪

542
00:22:36,148 --> 00:22:40,277
♪ We lie buried as we
glare into the distance ♪

543
00:22:40,652 --> 00:22:43,405
♪ I can't hear anything ♪

544
00:22:43,405 --> 00:22:46,325
♪ I can't seem to cut anything ♪

545
00:22:46,325 --> 00:22:49,161
♪ It feels like I'm sinking ♪

546
00:22:49,161 --> 00:22:51,038
♪ Falling, falling ♪

547
00:22:51,038 --> 00:22:52,122
♪ Touching ♪

548
00:22:52,122 --> 00:22:55,667
♪ Eyes struck wide open ♪

549
00:22:55,667 --> 00:22:59,004
♪ Something no one has ever seen ♪

550
00:22:59,004 --> 00:23:05,302
♪ The furthest reaches
are now visible to us ♪

551
00:23:05,302 --> 00:23:09,306
♪ It cannot be undone
and cannot be stopped ♪

552
00:23:09,306 --> 00:23:12,726
♪ This ensuing struggle ♪

553
00:23:12,726 --> 00:23:17,314
♪ Whisk it away beyond
the ends of the earth ♪

554
00:23:17,314 --> 00:23:19,358
♪ Along with our breaths ♪

555
00:23:19,816 --> 00:23:21,193
♪ Take everything ♪

556
00:23:21,193 --> 00:23:26,031
♪ Whisk it away beyond
the ends of the earth ♪

557
00:23:26,031 --> 00:23:28,033
♪ Along with our futures ♪

558
00:23:28,033 --> 00:23:29,743
♪ Along with our world ♪

559
00:23:30,827 --> 00:23:34,248
♪ Something no one has ever seen ♪

560
00:23:34,248 --> 00:23:40,629
♪ The furthest reaches
are now visible to us ♪

561
00:23:40,629 --> 00:23:42,589
♪ Don't you know God's demand? ♪

562
00:23:42,756 --> 00:23:44,424
♪ Don't you know God's demand? ♪

563
00:23:44,424 --> 00:23:48,053
♪ As we tear each other down. ♪

564
00:23:52,850 --> 00:23:54,142
[Ichibe] Hmm?

565
00:23:58,522 --> 00:24:02,943
Ah, so you're awake, Soul King.

566
00:24:03,819 --> 00:24:06,613
(mystical music)

567
00:24:11,326 --> 00:24:16,331
[Kenpachi] Neither form nor
soul will escape my blade.

568
00:24:16,707 --> 00:24:19,209
Nothing except you.

569
00:24:22,337 --> 00:24:27,342
-("Saihate" by SennaRin)
-(singing in Japanese)

